# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment  (NEVER commit these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json
secrets/

# Private SSH keys, by their conventional filenames. These have no extension,
# so the `*.pem` / `*.key` patterns above do not catch them. A pattern without
# a slash matches at any depth, so these also cover nested copies such as
# `.ssh/id_rsa`, `secrets/id_ed25519` or `deploy/id_ecdsa`.
#
# Public keys are deliberately NOT ignored: `id_rsa` does not match
# `id_rsa.pub`, and a public key is safe to commit when a deployment genuinely
# needs one.
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
id_ed25519_sk

# Generic credential files. `credentials.json` and `service-account*.json` are
# already covered above; this adds the `creds*.json` family (creds.json,
# creds-prod.json, creds_dev.json). Deliberately not a blanket `*.json`, which
# would hide package.json, tsconfig.json, test fixtures and OpenAPI output.
creds*.json

