# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database dumps and backups
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A dump taken from a real environment contains real data, so these must never
# be committed by accident. Targeted patterns rather than a blanket `*.sql`,
# so a deliberately reviewed statement file - `alembic upgrade head --sql`
# output, for instance - can still be added on purpose.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bz2
*.sql.xz
*.sql.zip
dump.sql
*-dump.sql
*_dump.sql
pg_dump*.sql
*.bak
backup/
backups/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime artefacts (generated by later phases)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
storage/
audio_storage/
*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.log
logs/

# One narrow exception to `*.wav`, kept narrow on purpose. The blanket rule
# above exists to stop captured call audio - which may carry a real person's
# voice - from ever being committed, and it stays. The files below are the
# opposite of that: synthesised by
# `backend/tests/fixtures/audio/generate.py`, deterministic, under 35 KB each,
# and containing no speech at all.
#
# They have to be tracked, or `pytest` cannot pass from a clean clone - the
# blanket rule silently excluded them, which is exactly the kind of omission
# that only shows up on somebody else's machine.
#
# Scoped to this one directory, so a stray recording anywhere else in the
# repository is still ignored. Do not broaden it, and never add a recording of
# a real call here - see that directory's README.
!backend/tests/fixtures/audio/*.wav

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Playwright MCP scratch output: page snapshots, console logs and network
# dumps written while driving the browser. Evidence that is worth keeping is
# committed deliberately under docs/, never from here.
.playwright-mcp/
